	(text "SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS (report, Table 'Requirements on the controlling system')\nR1-R12 and R14 are mandatory: the board's verification depends on them.\nR13 is recommended: it adds margin the verification does not count on.\n\nR1  Six PWM signals, complementary in pairs, 3.3 V CMOS, dead time >= 260 ns\n    generated by the peripheral\nR2  Enable low in every indeterminate state: reset, boot, watchdog\nR3  A DESAT fault is reset only by holding enable low for > 1 us\nR4  Modulation enabled only after the ready line goes high (all UVLO released)\nR5  Main contactor closes on the measured DC-link voltage, not on a timer\nR6  Differential ADC inputs, sampled synchronously with the carrier peak/valley\nR7  ADC trigger advanced by 3.1 us\nR8  Derating from the heat-sink thermistor\nR9  Interlock loop supervision and contactor command by the vehicle\nR10 Galvanic isolation in the charging path (on-board AC or in the DC station)\nR11 Source impedance at 20 kHz: L >= 1.5 uH or R >= 50 mOhm\nR12 Max continuous battery voltage 900 V; up to 1000 V only with the bridge\n    disabled and for < 30 min a day\nR13 (recommended) Below a few hertz of output frequency, DPWM-MAX: clamp to the\n    positive rail the phase carrying the largest positive current\nR14 Coolant at the rail inlet: 50/50 water-glycol, <= 65 C, >= 10 l/min"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.00 25.00 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.50 1.50)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c7218d1c-a8de-40bd-a04d-6616fdc410ad")
	)
